messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2025,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2027,
      "event": "AI agents routinely complete multi-day professional tasks with little supervision.",
      "detail": "Software engineering, research assistance and office work are the first fields to be heavily automated. Productivity gains are real but uneven."
    },
    {
      "year": 2029,
      "event": "Humans land on the Moon again.",
      "detail": "The United States or China, and probably both within a few years, return crews to the lunar surface and start building a semi-permanent base."
    },
    {
      "year": 2032,
      "event": "AI systems match or exceed human experts at nearly all cognitive work.",
      "detail": "The exact date is uncertain by a decade or more, but this is the pivotal transition of the century. AI begins to substantially speed up its own development."
    },
    {
      "year": 2034,
      "event": "Global warming passes 1.5°C above pre-industrial levels on a sustained basis.",
      "detail": "Heat waves, fires, floods and crop shocks worsen. Emissions are falling but too slowly to meet the Paris targets."
    },
    {
      "year": 2037,
      "event": "A serious AI-related crisis forces binding international controls on advanced AI.",
      "detail": "A large-scale misuse or loss-of-control incident, such as a cyberattack, a bioweapon attempt or a rogue system, causes major harm. This is also the period of highest risk of an unrecoverable catastrophe."
    },
    {
      "year": 2040,
      "event": "General-purpose robots automate most physical labor in advanced economies.",
      "detail": "Combined with AI-run research, economic growth and scientific discovery far outpace historical rates. Most people no longer need to work, and wealth and power concentrate dangerously."
    },
    {
      "year": 2043,
      "event": "A severe pandemic, natural or engineered, is contained by AI-designed countermeasures.",
      "detail": "Cheap biotechnology makes outbreaks more likely, but vaccines and treatments are designed and produced in weeks. The death toll is far below what it would have been in the 2020s."
    },
    {
      "year": 2048,
      "event": "The first humans land on Mars.",
      "detail": "Robotic pre-deployment makes the mission possible. It is mainly symbolic, since machines do almost all the useful work in space."
    },
    {
      "year": 2052,
      "event": "Most countries adopt some form of guaranteed income funded by automated production.",
      "detail": "Human employment becomes largely optional. Societies struggle with questions of meaning, status and political power in a world run mostly by AI."
    },
    {
      "year": 2058,
      "event": "Therapies that slow and partly reverse aging become widely available.",
      "detail": "Healthy life expectancy begins to rise by more than one year per year for those with access. Access spreads worldwide over the following decades."
    },
    {
      "year": 2065,
      "event": "Fossil fuels are largely phased out as solar, fission and fusion make energy abundant.",
      "detail": "Net global emissions approach zero. Cheap energy makes large-scale carbon removal and desalination practical."
    },
    {
      "year": 2075,
      "event": "Global temperature peaks at roughly 2 to 2.5°C above pre-industrial levels.",
      "detail": "Active carbon removal begins to lower atmospheric CO2. Many ecosystems and coastlines are already permanently changed."
    },
    {
      "year": 2090,
      "event": "Digital minds vastly outnumber biological humans and gain legal standing.",
      "detail": "These include AIs and probably the first emulated human brains. Their rights and votes become the central political issue."
    },
    {
      "year": 2120,
      "event": "Self-sustaining industrial settlements operate on the Moon, Mars and asteroids.",
      "detail": "They are built and run mainly by machines, with human populations in the thousands to low millions. Space-based industry begins to exceed Earth's."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "The biological human population stabilizes, with most people enhanced.",
      "detail": "Low birth rates are offset by very long lifespans. Genetic and neural enhancement are normal, and the line between human and machine intelligence is blurred."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "The first interstellar probes are launched at a meaningful fraction of light speed.",
      "detail": "Small self-replicating probes head for nearby stars. The solar system economy is thousands of times larger than the economy of 2025."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Sea level is between one and a few meters above the 2000 level.",
      "detail": "Slow ice-sheet response continues even though temperatures are falling. Coastal cities have been moved, protected or abandoned."
    },
    {
      "year": 2350,
      "event": "Probes arrive at Alpha Centauri and begin building infrastructure.",
      "detail": "Self-replicating machines construct receivers, habitats and computing facilities. Minds can then travel there as transmitted data."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "A partial Dyson swarm captures a noticeable share of the Sun's output.",
      "detail": "Most of civilization's activity is computation in space habitats. Earth holds a small share of the total population of minds."
    },
    {
      "year": 2700,
      "event": "A major conflict or systemic failure damages part of solar-system civilization.",
      "detail": "Over centuries, some large-scale war, ideological split or cascading technical failure is likely. Recovery is fast because knowledge and industry are widely distributed."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Settlements are established in dozens of star systems within about 30 light-years.",
      "detail": "Inhabitants are overwhelmingly digital or heavily engineered beings. Communication delays of years to decades make each system effectively self-governing."
    },
    {
      "year": 3300,
      "event": "Unmodified biological humans are a tiny, protected minority.",
      "detail": "Some communities choose to remain close to the original human form, mostly on Earth. They are kept safe much like a cultural heritage."
    },
    {
      "year": 3800,
      "event": "Earth is managed as a restored biosphere and heritage world.",
      "detail": "CO2 and climate are deliberately regulated, and many extinct species have been recreated. Heavy industry left the planet long ago."
    },
    {
      "year": 4500,
      "event": "The settled region extends more than 100 light-years from the Sun.",
      "detail": "Expansion continues at a modest fraction of light speed. Distant branches diverge in culture, values and physical form."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "The Dyson swarm captures most of the Sun's energy.",
      "detail": "The home system supports an enormous population of minds. Technology is close to the limits set by known physics, and progress becomes mostly cultural."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "There is no longer a single humanity, only many descendant lineages.",
      "detail": "Light-speed delays prevent any unified government or culture. Some branches would be unrecognizable or disturbing to people today."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "Surveys of thousands of star systems have found no other technological civilization.",
      "detail": "Simple life may have been found elsewhere, but intelligent neighbors most likely have not. This suggests our descendants are alone in this part of the galaxy."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "The expansion front is roughly 500 to 1,000 light-years from Earth.",
      "detail": "Millions of star systems are occupied or being developed. Occasional conflicts between divergent branches occur but cannot spread quickly across such distances."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Large-scale stellar engineering is under way to store resources for the far future.",
      "detail": "Some branches reshape stars and stockpile matter and energy for use over trillions of years. Others focus on preservation, art or inner experience."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Descendants of humanity occupy a region about a thousand light-years across.",
      "detail": "A small population of recognizable humans probably still lives on Earth and elsewhere. The vast majority of minds are digital or engineered beings descended from humans and their AIs."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "uncertain",
  "summary": "I think the most likely path is that humanity survives the dangerous transition to advanced AI in this century and its descendants spread into space, with biological humans becoming a small, protected minority among digital and engineered minds. However, I put perhaps a one-in-four chance on extinction or permanent loss of human control, mostly within the next two centuries, so no single extinction year appears on the timeline. All dates beyond about 2100 are very rough guesses."
}
